    <AuContent>
      <AuHeading @level="1" @skin="1">About this Smart Search and data</AuHeading>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">What this tool does</AuHeading>
      <p>
        DECIDe Smart Search lets you ask a question in your own words about decisions and regulations published by a
        local authority. Your question is compared to the decisions in the DECIDe data space, and the most relevant ones
        are passed to an AI language model, which writes an answer based on those documents. The answer always shows
        which decisions it is based on, so you can read the original yourself.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">What we store</AuHeading>
      <p>For every question asked, we store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the local authority you selected</li>
        <li>the question you typed</li>
        <li>the full instruction sent to the AI model</li>
        <li>the generated answer</li>
        <li>the decisions used as sources, and how relevant each one was</li>
        <li>your thumbs up or thumbs down on the answer and on the individual sources</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not ask you to log in and we do not link questions to an account or to your identity.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">Why we store it</AuHeading>
      <p>DECIDe is a pilot project. We store questions and answers for three reasons:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong class="au-u-medium">Quality control.</strong>
          We check whether the system finds the right decisions and gives correct answers. Your thumbs up or down is the
          main signal we use for this.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="au-u-medium">Improving the service.</strong>
          Recurring questions tell us where the search or the underlying data falls short.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="au-u-medium">Project evaluation.</strong>
          The results feed into the reporting and research on which the project is assessed.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        We do not use this data for advertising, profiling, or any decision that affects you personally. The stored
        questions and answers are not published as open data.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">How long we keep it</AuHeading>
      <p>
        Questions, answers and validations are kept for one year, after which they are deleted.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">Why you should not enter personal data</AuHeading>
      <p>
        Because we store what you type, anything personal you include is stored too, and it may be read by the project
        team during quality checks. Please avoid:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>names of people, your own or someone else's</li>
        <li>addresses, phone numbers, email addresses</li>
        <li>national register numbers, file or case numbers</li>
        <li>health, financial or family details</li>
        <li>anything else that could identify a person</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You do not need any of this to get a good answer. Ask about the situation, not about the person. For example,
        ask "What subsidies exist for roof insulation?" instead of "Can [name] at [address] get a subsidy for their
        roof?" The first question gives you exactly the same result.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">A note on the answers</AuHeading>
      <p>
        The answers are generated by an AI model. They can be incomplete or wrong. Always check the source decisions
        listed under the answer before you act on it. This tool is not legal advice and has no legal status.
      </p>

      <AuHeading @level="2" @skin="3">Your rights and contact</AuHeading>
      <p>
        You have the right to ask what data we hold about you, to have it corrected, and to have it deleted. Because we
        do not link questions to an identity, we may need extra information from you to trace a specific question.
      </p>
      <p>The controller for this processing is:</p>
      <p>
        Agentschap Binnenlands Bestuur<br />
        Herman Teirlinckgebouw<br />
        Havenlaan 88 bus 70<br />
        1000 Brussels, Belgium
      </p>
      <p>
        You can reach the Data Protection Officer at
        <a class="au-c-link" href="mailto:teamDPO-ABB@vlaanderen.be">teamDPO-ABB@vlaanderen.be</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe data has not been handled correctly, you can lodge a complaint with the supervisory
        authority:
      </p>
      <p>
        Vlaamse Toezichtcommissie voor de verwerking van persoonsgegevens (VTC)<br />
